00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.527
(Drew laughing)

00:02:23.298 --> 00:02:28.298
Oh my God, thank you, thank you.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:29.948
I don't-

00:02:30.927 --> 00:02:32.850
I don't know if anyone got a glimpse

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:36.580
of the beginning of season one,

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:40.630
but I went real hard by myself here.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:41.660
I looked nuts.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.660
We were all nuts.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.640
It was September of 2020.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.710
We had this really intimate setting,

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:48.950
and yet one day we hoped

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:51.280
that maybe we could ever get here.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.210
So to our very first New
York studio audience,

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:59.340
thank you so much!
(audience applause)

00:03:02.798 --> 00:03:05.129
Thank you, thank you so much.

00:03:05.129 --> 00:03:08.129
(audience cheering)

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:11.287
It's a total dream.

00:03:11.287 --> 00:03:13.070
One I never thought we'd get to,

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:15.700
but here we are in our season two,

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:19.040
and it is such a privilege to be back

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.000
in my new hometown of New York.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:27.270
I love it here so much.
(audience applause)

00:03:28.645 --> 00:03:30.100
I don't know if you can
tell from my accent,

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.780
but I'm from California.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:32.613
(audience laughing)

00:03:32.613 --> 00:03:36.390
And we're just celebrating
everything about hometowns.

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:39.570
We kicked off in my
hometown of Los Angeles,

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:42.810
and we're here now, and you know,

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:45.370
I just want to celebrate the whole country

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:49.510
and celebrate the fact that
there is no place like home.

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:51.370
And that emotional storytelling for me

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:54.500
is gonna be a huge thread for this season.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.732
And we actually get to leave the studio.

00:03:56.732 --> 00:04:00.420
So I want to take it as far vast and wide

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.030
as they'll possibly let us,

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:04.640
and here we are, starting in New York.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.840
And our first guest couldn't be more true

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:13.660
to the storytelling and the
thematic nature of New York

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:16.970
because she hails from Queens.

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:20.120
She is a rapper, a Golden Globe winner,

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.470
and you know, superstar from like,

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:25.460
blockbuster hits like "Crazy Rich Asians."

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:27.304
I know!
(audience cheering)

00:04:27.304 --> 00:04:29.630
Isn't that the best movie ever?

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:32.130
I have seen that movie 50 times.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:35.130
She's in the amazing movie "Farewell,"

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:37.840
for which she won a Golden Globe.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.430
And she's most recently

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:44.150
in the number one film across
the entire globe, "Shang-Chi."

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:48.193
So, I know.
(audience applause)

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:51.710
Her star just continues to rise,

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:55.250
and you can catch her on
her show on Comedy Central,

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:57.940
which I love so much, "Nora From Queens."

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.290
Take a look.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.143
- We are hot.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:05.313
- I look more like Owen
Wilson than I do Cameron Diaz.

00:05:06.348 --> 00:05:11.348
- Selfie!

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:13.790
- Who's gonna take it?

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:14.623
- Oh.

00:05:14.623 --> 00:05:15.840
- Okay we literally
don't have time for this.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.091
We have 23 stops tonight, let's go.

00:05:18.091 --> 00:05:20.252
- How many stops?
- 23!

00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:22.414
- (laughing) I love it!
(audience applause)

00:05:22.414 --> 00:05:25.294
Please welcome Awkwafina!

00:05:25.294 --> 00:05:27.502
(audience applause)

00:05:27.502 --> 00:05:29.002
- Yeah! What's up!

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:32.446
Hey!
- Hello!

00:05:32.446 --> 00:05:33.279
- Hi Drew!

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:36.800
Yes!
- Oh my God.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.837
I love this.
- New York in the building.

00:05:38.837 --> 00:05:41.140
- Right! I mean, Queens!

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:43.600
You are a queen, and you're from Queens.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:46.565
That's fitting.
- Yeah, appreciate that.

00:05:46.565 --> 00:05:47.398
That's good.
- You know,

00:05:47.398 --> 00:05:49.075
another queen from Queens,

00:05:49.075 --> 00:05:51.143
is Lucy Liu.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.590
And I wanted to ask you,

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:59.110
because Lucy had meaning
for you back in the day,

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:02.600
and I would just love
to hear from you, like,

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:06.640
what that was because I
love her and I love you,

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.275
and so I'm like, in the middle,

00:06:08.275 --> 00:06:12.870
just wanting to know how
that story came about.

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.540
- Lucy Liu was, and "Charlie's Angels,"

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:20.060
was like the pinnacle of
like, everything to me,

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:24.620
and to see Lucy in a role like that

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:26.260
was really momentous.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:29.220
It changed the way that I
looked at myself and the world.

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:31.853
And I will say that I don't think

00:06:31.853 --> 00:06:34.320
that I would be where I am, truly,

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:39.000
without seeing Lucy Liu do
her thing back in the day.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:39.833
It's good.

00:06:39.833 --> 00:06:41.540
- When I watch "Nora From Queens,"

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.620
and your storytelling is so strong,

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:47.870
the way, you know, humor
to me has to have heart.

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:51.000
It's like, but I want humor to push.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.410
How do you have the bravery
to push that humor so far,

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:55.550
'cause you go there.

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:56.550
You don't compromise.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:57.860
You're such a badass.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:58.900
- You know, I agree.

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:00.840
I think all humor needs to have

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:02.360
kind of heart at its baseline.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:05.591
A lot of the things that
I talk about in my show

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:08.270
are a mixture of reality or like,

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:10.300
what I would imagine, you know,

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:14.780
my family or what they would say.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.180
So I try to stick to that.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:19.790
- What's so amazing is in
that very same episode,

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:21.270
you will break my heart,

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:23.560
and make me emotional, you know,

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:26.560
when you talk about your grandma.

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:30.040
And you did grow up in
Queens with your grandma.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:33.840
And will you tell us about
that time of your life?

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:37.300
- She was definitely not, you know,

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:38.600
your ordinary parent.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:39.433
I think, like, you know,

00:07:39.433 --> 00:07:42.177
she really kind of
noticed the spunk in me,

00:07:42.177 --> 00:07:44.750
and I remember I always
used to ask her, like,

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:45.990
I feel weird, grandma.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:47.350
I feel like I don't fit in.

00:07:47.350 --> 00:07:48.935
I feel like, you know,

00:07:48.935 --> 00:07:51.510
people think certain things about me,

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:52.930
and I just feel weird.

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:56.583
And she always told me
the weirdness in you

00:07:56.583 --> 00:07:58.667
is inevitably what's
gonna make you different

00:07:58.667 --> 00:07:59.810
and what's gonna make you special.

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:00.643
She always told me that.

00:08:00.643 --> 00:08:02.490
You know, she was always a big fan,

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:04.110
but she was also, you know,

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:06.260
like we got into shenanigans together

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:09.191
as well, you know.

00:08:09.191 --> 00:08:12.980
There was a carnival that would
come to town, for instance,

00:08:12.980 --> 00:08:15.190
and she didn't want to
pay the admissions fee.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:16.920
So they gave out these bracelets

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:19.220
with little designs on them.

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:21.411
And she was like, let's just
buy a marker and white paper,

00:08:21.411 --> 00:08:23.420
and I'll just tape it to your arm,

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:25.630
and we'll make your admission bracelet,

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:28.321
so I don't gotta pay like
ten bucks to get you in.

00:08:28.321 --> 00:08:30.130
(laughing)

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:31.900
- I love that story so much.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:34.250
And isn't it true when you were like 16,

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:37.080
she also told you something?

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.720
- She'd be like, you're ten years old

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.570
so that we can go to the buffet

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:42.547
and you can get a child discount.

00:08:42.547 --> 00:08:44.451
(audience laughing)

00:08:44.451 --> 00:08:46.580
And she literally would like,

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:49.551
slap a backwards cap on me, and it's like,

00:08:49.551 --> 00:08:53.580
what is a backwards cap
just code for I'm a kid?

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:55.870
- Yes.
- But it worked.

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:56.703
- Okay.
(audience applause)

00:08:56.703 --> 00:09:00.530
Another total juxtaposition with something

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:03.310
I was hoping that you could
share with our audience

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:06.150
because I just thought
it was such a hot tip,

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:07.830
and we could all benefit from it.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:10.730
It's a beauty tip that you
gave to Allure Magazine

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:13.880
with your gorgeous cover that
was so unique and dynamic.

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:16.460
- Thank you, absolutely.

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:20.050
So if you ever need a makeup blotter,

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:21.560
or like a face blotter,

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.330
just go to any airport,

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:26.120
and just take a toilet seat cover.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:28.220
Because that's what that is.
(audience laughing)

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:29.443
Yes, girl!

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:32.560
Yes, you could put your
head through it, too.

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:35.287
That's a necklace.
- It's true, you could.

00:09:35.287 --> 00:09:36.500
- Yes, girl.
(audience laughing)

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:39.560
- And then you could actually-
- And make it fashion.

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:41.870
- And then...
- There you go.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:42.960
And it's a bib!

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.790
- You changed my life with this tip,

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:46.650
so I just want to thank you.

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:50.679
'Cause I'm never looking at
these suckers the same way.

00:09:50.679 --> 00:09:54.762
(audience laughing and clapping)

00:09:57.020 --> 00:09:59.860
We're gonna go to a quick
commercial break, if that's okay.

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:01.960
And when we come back, I'd like to play

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:04.050
a little game with you, Awkwafina.

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:06.055
Beautiful Nora.
- I would love.

00:10:06.055 --> 00:10:09.870
- With someone else who's a
very special Queens native,

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:11.910
and I'm very excited about this.

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:13.733
We'll be right back.
(upbeat music)

00:10:13.733 --> 00:10:16.733
(audience applause)

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.950
I thought you should play against

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:22.280
