00:12:57.390 --> 00:13:00.610
Yes, oh my god, so cool.
- By the way, Fran,

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:03.260
I was reading something
that you said once.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:05.360
Is it true that like,

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:07.910
one television executive
said to you, like,

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:10.350
your voice, I don't know.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.630
And then another person was like,

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:15.720
it's because of you, your
voice, your personality,

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:17.640
that this is gonna work.

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:20.330
- Yes, actually, you know, I mean,

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:22.470
all along the road,

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:26.600
people said that the voice
was going to hold me back.

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:30.500
And it was Peter Jacobsen,
my writing producing partner

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:35.160
and my beloved gay
ex-husband who said, uh uh,

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:37.910
that's, you know, the voice, the face,

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:41.100
the comic timing, that's
what's gonna make you a star.

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:43.320
And we're gonna lean into it.

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:45.560
We're not gonna try and dilute it

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:48.050
or move away from it.

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:50.300
And he was right, you
know, I'm really grateful.

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:54.620
But back in the day when we
had sold the idea for the show,

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:55.957
they actually said,

00:13:55.957 --> 00:13:58.920
"Can the character be
Italian and not Jewish?"

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:00.090
- [Drew] Right.

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:03.124
And you said no.
- And yeah we,

00:14:03.124 --> 00:14:04.580
we said no, because you know,

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:07.150
we couldn't write it as authentically.

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:09.500
I know how to be Jewish.

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:11.310
We know how to write Jewish.
(audience laughing)

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:12.730
That's the way we have to go,

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:15.900
and I kind of just, even though
I knew it was my big break,

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:17.790
we said, you know, no,

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.900
because I don't like to have regret.

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:23.950
And I thought, if I go along
with this idiotic suggestion

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:25.590
and it doesn't fly,

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:26.910
I'm gonna be kicking myself.

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:28.180
Why did I listen to them?

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:31.130
So you know, I just kind
of make it a cardinal rule

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:32.770
that I go with my gut,

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:34.570
and I try and convince everybody

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:36.393
why I think it's the right idea.

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:39.450
Rather than have to play it, please.

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:42.220
- Well I thank you both
for putting out shows

00:14:42.220 --> 00:14:44.390
authentic to who you are,

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:47.580
and changing the world
to welcome other people

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:50.090
to find that confidence and do the same.

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:51.470
So thank you for that, seriously.

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:53.063
- Thank you.
(audience applause)

00:14:53.063 --> 00:14:54.667
Yeah, we always had, thank you.

00:14:54.667 --> 00:14:58.630
- And, so your origin
story starts in Queens.

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:00.130
We're gonna play a game.

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:03.320
You guys are gonna take
turns answering questions

00:15:03.320 --> 00:15:05.690
with multiple choice options,

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:07.980
and the person with the
most correct answers

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:09.630
wins the "Queen of Queens."

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:10.463
Let's get to it.

00:15:10.463 --> 00:15:12.039
The first question goes to Awkwafina.

00:15:12.039 --> 00:15:14.470
Awkwafina, what famous magician

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:17.290
is buried in a cemetery in Queens?

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:20.410
Is it A, David Copperfield,

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:23.730
B, William Ellsworth Robinson,

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:28.730
C, magicians can't always be
put in a box, they can escape,

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:30.880
or D, Harry Houdini.

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:31.960
- I want to say Houdini,

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:35.373
but I feel like it might
be Copperfield, or C.

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:38.680
Oh god, the magicians
are gonna come after me.

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:41.140
The magicians are gonna come, Houdini.

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:43.462
- Okay, well it's Harry Houdini.

00:15:43.462 --> 00:15:44.540
- Okay it's Harry Houdini!

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:47.319
It's Harry Houdini.
(audience applause)

00:15:47.319 --> 00:15:48.700
(bright music)

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:49.533
- Oh, look.

00:15:49.533 --> 00:15:51.690
She's got crowns falling from the sky.

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:53.940
Okay Fran, what neighborhood of Queens

00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:55.630
did Cindy Lauper grow up in?

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:57.930
Was it Ozone Park, A,

00:15:57.930 --> 00:15:59.510
B, Jackson Heights,

00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:02.120
C, girls just want to have Flushing,

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:04.023
or D, Sunnyside?

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:07.120
- I'm gonna say Ozone Park.
(bell dings)

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:09.271
- You are right!
(audience applause)

00:16:09.271 --> 00:16:12.940
- Whoa, whoa, yes, yes!

00:16:15.673 --> 00:16:17.190
Yes!
- Okay, Awkwafina.

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:19.890
Which one of these people of note

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:22.520
was not born in Queens?

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:24.510
A, Howard Stern,

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:26.650
B, Tony Danza,

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:28.570
C, Lori Laughlin,

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:30.213
or D, Al Roker.

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:32.703
- Oh, oh man.

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:37.870
I almost want to say, Howard Stern,

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:40.580
but I don't know, I don't know.

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:41.820
Can I have a lifeline?
(audience laughing)

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:43.023
Can I take a lifeline?

00:16:43.023 --> 00:16:44.968
Fran, what do you think?

00:16:44.968 --> 00:16:46.300
Who do you think it is?

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:48.920
- I think your first instincts are right.

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:51.040
I'm gonna say Howard Stern.

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:53.070
- Well, you'll both be interested to know

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:55.060
it's B, Tony Danza.
(buzzer buzzing)

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:57.675
He was not born in Queens.

00:16:57.675 --> 00:16:58.508
- [Fran] Oh.

00:16:58.508 --> 00:16:59.903
- He was born in Brooklyn.

00:17:01.023 --> 00:17:01.856
Okay, Fran's turn.

00:17:01.856 --> 00:17:04.310
Which subway line runs through Queens?

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:05.540
A, the 6 Train,

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:06.810
B, the D Train,

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:08.500
C, the A Train,

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.390
D, IDK.

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:12.443
- I'm gonna guess the D.

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:15.123
No?
(Buzzer buzzing)

00:17:15.123 --> 00:17:17.040
- It is the A train.

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:19.620
- The A Train goes to Queens?

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:21.123
- Apparently.

00:17:21.123 --> 00:17:23.520
- It does, it goes.
- Alright.

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:26.040
The score is tied.
- It has been a while

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:27.620
since I've taken the subway.
(audience laughing)

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:32.620
You know, I've been stuck
in a train car with fans.

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:34.785
There's no way out, you know.

00:17:34.785 --> 00:17:36.061
(audience laughing)

00:17:36.061 --> 00:17:37.820
- No, no.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.630
Okay the last question goes to Awkwafina.

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:43.230
What part of Queens did
The Nanny take place in?

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:44.700
A, Astoria,

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:46.050
B, Forest Hills,

00:17:46.050 --> 00:17:47.800
C, Flushing,

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:52.800
D, Drescher Island.
(audience laughing)

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:54.718
- C, right?

00:17:54.718 --> 00:17:56.416
- Yes! Yes!
(bell dings)

00:17:56.416 --> 00:17:58.713
- Yes!
- Flushing, you got it!

00:17:58.713 --> 00:17:59.733
(audience applause)

00:17:59.733 --> 00:18:01.184
- Thank you.

00:18:01.184 --> 00:18:03.560
- I'm the flashy girl from Flushing.

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:06.838
- The flashy girl from
Flushing, the nanny named Fran.

00:18:06.838 --> 00:18:11.110
- Well, the accumulative
winner is Awkwafina today.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:15.740
But you are both queens,
two amazing queens,

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:19.037
who have changed the world.
(audience applause)

00:18:19.037 --> 00:18:21.454
- Three queens, three queens.

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:26.880
- Awkwafina and Fran Drescher,

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:31.544
I am so honored to be in your
Queens sandwich right now.

00:18:31.544 --> 00:18:33.160
- Thank you.
- And may we all be able

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:35.367
to come together again
as soon as possible.

00:18:35.367 --> 00:18:38.820
"Nora From Queens" wednesdays
at 10:00, 9:00 Central

00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:40.760
on Comedy Central.

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:43.480
And the wonderful,
magnanimous Fran Drescher.

00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:44.913
Thank you, we'll be right back.

00:18:44.913 --> 00:18:47.162
Thank you! Thank you!
(upbeat music)

00:18:47.162 --> 00:18:50.162
(audience applause)

00:18:57.305 --> 00:18:59.990
(upbeat music)

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:02.810
All season long, we're
highlighting hometowns

00:19:02.810 --> 00:19:04.761
all across the country because

00:19:04.761 --> 00:19:07.580
there's no place like home.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:10.060
Next up, it's Seattle, Washington,

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:14.020
where Marlie and Anthony Love call home.

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:15.590
The Loves love Seattle,

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:18.710
and I have a feeling we're about to, also.

00:19:18.710 --> 00:19:19.583
Watch this.

00:19:21.070 --> 00:19:23.130
- Hey Drew, it's Anthony and Marlie,

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:24.890
and we're in front of Pike Place Market.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:26.970
Located in our hometown
of Seattle, Washington.

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:29.390
- Drew, we love Seattle so much.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:32.430
Not just because of the great
scenery and great coffee,

00:19:32.430 --> 00:19:35.100
but there's some places that
mean so much to us personally.

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:38.250
- So, come with us and
let us show you around.

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:40.833
(upbeat music)

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:44.370
- We are at the iconic Space Needle.

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:47.200
A signature staple for
the Seattle skyline.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:48.580
- Of course it's iconic,

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:50.770
but it's personal for us because

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:53.720
on my first trip to Seattle in 2015,

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:55.270
this was the spot

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:58.590
when we decided that we
were gonna move to Seattle.

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:01.360
- And now it just represents
the love that we have

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:02.253
for this city.

00:20:03.546 --> 00:20:05.310
(upbeat music)

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:07.260
Welcome to Boon Boona Coffee.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:09.450
Boon Boona is a local Seattle coffee shop

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:11.920
that specializes in African coffee.

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:13.570
- Before moving to Seattle,

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:15.860
we only drank the name brand stuff.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:17.490
But locals told us, hey,

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:19.280
you have to try a local spot.

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:22.580
Boon Boona was the first
one, and we fell in love.

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:23.860
- Now that got some coffee,

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:26.785
let us take you to another
spot that is personal to us.

00:20:26.785 --> 00:20:29.160
(upbeat music)

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.357
- We're in front of Alki Beach.

00:20:30.357 --> 00:20:33.500
One of many beaches located
right here in Seattle.

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:35.950
- Yeah, there's so many
beautiful beaches in Seattle.

00:20:35.950 --> 00:20:37.470
You really can't go wrong.

00:20:37.470 --> 00:20:39.890
But Alki is our personal favorite.

00:20:39.890 --> 00:20:41.910
Not only because it was the first beach

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:43.860
that we visited when we moved to Seattle,

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:46.620
but look at those breathtaking views.

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:49.970
- [Anthony] Also, visitors can
play volleyball, walk, run,

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:52.960
or ride on the paved path
laid along the beach.

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:54.100
- [Marlie] On top of all that,

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:55.810
right across from the
beach are great options

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:57.070
for food and fun.

00:20:57.070 --> 00:20:59.310
With plenty of restaurants,
bars, and shops.

00:20:59.310 --> 00:21:02.293
Alki Beach, another reason
why we love Seattle.

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:06.180
- Well Drew, that's just a snapshot

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:08.170
of this beautiful city of Seattle.

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:10.180
- We hope you love it as much as we do.

00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:11.770
We can't wait for you to come visit!

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:12.603
See you soon.

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:15.680
- I love you, Loves!

00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:18.140
And by the way, I never go to Seattle

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:19.970
without hitting Pike's Market

00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:23.440
and having a bowl of the
best clam chowder ever.

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:25.130
Ah, what a wonderful place.

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:27.360
I love Seattle, and hometowns,

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:29.335
and I love this country.

00:21:29.335 --> 00:21:31.918
(upbeat music)

00:21:35.348 --> 00:21:40.348
(upbeat music)
(audience applause)

00:21:42.115 --> 00:21:43.500
Hello, welcome back.

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:47.830
Our next guest became a
viral sensation on TikTok

00:21:47.830 --> 00:21:49.410
for breaking into someone's home,

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:51.180
but it's not what you're thinking,

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:53.270
'cause we're not advocating that here.

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:55.790
He didn't actually take
anything from the house,

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:57.350
not even a little.

00:21:57.350 --> 00:21:59.220
But he did leave it spotless,

00:21:59.220 --> 00:22:01.470
after spending two and
a half hours cleaning it

00:22:01.470 --> 00:22:03.130
from top to bottom.

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:05.050
Yeah, I know, this is such a wild story.

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:05.883
Check this out.

00:22:06.923 --> 00:22:07.756
(upbeat music)

00:22:07.756 --> 00:22:09.180
- So, my friend tells me

00:22:09.180 --> 00:22:11.112
that one of his coworkers

00:22:11.112 --> 00:22:13.040
wants me to clean his apartment.

00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:14.830
So I go there today,

00:22:14.830 --> 00:22:18.180
and he tells me that
there's a key under the mat.

00:22:18.180 --> 00:22:20.500
Get the key, go into the apartment,

00:22:20.500 --> 00:22:22.150
clean the entire apartment.

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:24.520
So he calls me and he's like,

00:22:24.520 --> 00:22:26.037
yo, where are you?

00:22:26.037 --> 00:22:28.320
And I was like, um,
I'm in your living room

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:29.340
waiting for you to walk in.

00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:31.350
I'm playing with your cat.

00:22:31.350 --> 00:22:34.947
He goes, "Man, I don't have a cat."

00:22:35.845 --> 00:22:36.678
What?

00:22:37.680 --> 00:22:41.540
So, comes to find out that I
cleaned the wrong apartment,

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:45.470
and broke in and cleaned
somebody's random apartment.

00:22:45.470 --> 00:22:46.303
You're welcome?

00:22:47.397 --> 00:22:48.440
(audience laughing)

00:22:48.440 --> 00:22:50.653
- Please say hello to Louie Angelino!

00:22:50.653 --> 00:22:53.653
(audience applause)

00:22:56.243 --> 00:22:57.540
So, how did this happen?

00:22:57.540 --> 00:22:59.250
- So, I was off by one digit.

00:22:59.250 --> 00:23:00.543
It was only one number.

00:23:01.557 --> 00:23:03.327
227 instead of 277.

00:23:04.513 --> 00:23:08.570
And I had just assumed that I was going

00:23:08.570 --> 00:23:10.253
to the right address.

00:23:11.170 --> 00:23:13.500
But it just so happened that

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:16.510
there was two keys under both of the mats,

00:23:16.510 --> 00:23:18.090
which is insane,

00:23:18.090 --> 00:23:19.510
because what are the odds

00:23:19.510 --> 00:23:21.950
that there's going to be two keys

00:23:21.950 --> 00:23:24.490
on the same time in the same day

00:23:24.490 --> 00:23:26.274
under both mats?

00:23:26.274 --> 00:23:27.780
- How did you even get in

00:23:27.780 --> 00:23:30.163
to the taking care of people's homes?

00:23:31.280 --> 00:23:32.160
- To be completely honest,

00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:34.240
with everything that happened with COVID,

00:23:34.240 --> 00:23:37.000
I was feeling very uninspired,

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:40.470
and she's in the audience right now,

00:23:40.470 --> 00:23:42.530
is my best friend, Jo Duran's mom,

00:23:42.530 --> 00:23:44.020
and my mother are in the office.

00:23:44.020 --> 00:23:46.943
- Oh hi!
(audience applause)

00:23:47.800 --> 00:23:48.770
- That is them.

00:23:48.770 --> 00:23:52.760
They are the ones that, my
mom, ever since I was a kid,

00:23:52.760 --> 00:23:56.550
has always told me,
clean room, clean mind.

00:23:56.550 --> 00:24:00.486
And Diana, who looks so lovely today,

00:24:00.486 --> 00:24:04.530
told me, she came up with the idea

00:24:04.530 --> 00:24:07.890
to pay me like 50 bucks a week

00:24:07.890 --> 00:24:10.792
to just to keep the
apartment clean for her

00:24:10.792 --> 00:24:14.320
and my best friend, and
started out with that.

00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:16.200
And through doing that,

00:24:16.200 --> 00:24:17.400
I would just, you know,

00:24:17.400 --> 00:24:19.860
I would go in there with
my Bluetooth speaker,

00:24:19.860 --> 00:24:22.140
and I'm jamming out and I'm dancing,

00:24:22.140 --> 00:24:24.960
and I'm Swiffering, and
I'm having so much fun

00:24:24.960 --> 00:24:26.770
I don't even realize that I'm cleaning.

00:24:26.770 --> 00:24:29.920
I was at a very dark place at that time.

00:24:29.920 --> 00:24:32.210
I didn't have a car, I didn't have a job.

00:24:32.210 --> 00:24:33.920
I really didn't have a purpose.

00:24:33.920 --> 00:24:36.130
And they gave me that.

00:24:36.130 --> 00:24:40.620
- Thank you guys so much for
giving that type of advice

